# ${name}

A web application on the xtr packages: FastAPI, served from the same kernel as its console, with
a database, a message bus, an HTTP client, notifications and security configured.

## Run

```sh
docker compose up -d database   # the PostgreSQL DATABASE_URL points at
uv run ${name}-web              # serve on WEB_HOST:WEB_PORT, 127.0.0.1:8000 by default
uv run ${name}                  # every console command
uv run ${name} debug:router     # the routes
uv run ${name} debug:bundles    # the bundles and whether each is active
```

The environment is read from `.env`, then `.env.local`, then `.env.<APP_ENV>` and
`.env.<APP_ENV>.local`; a variable set in the shell wins. Keep machine-specific values in
`.env.local`, which is not committed. `DATABASE_URL` points at the PostgreSQL `compose.yaml`
runs, published on this machine by `compose.override.yaml`; `MESSENGER_DSN` at a RabbitMQ on this
machine. Nothing connects to either until it is used.

## Layout

```
src/${app}/
├── __main__.py        the console entry point
├── kernel.py          the kernel every entry point builds, and the environment loader
├── config/
│   ├── bundles.py     the active bundles — written by xtr-recipes
│   └── packages/      one @configure module per bundle
├── command/           the console commands
└── web/
    ├── __main__.py    the web entry point
    ├── app.py         the FastAPI application, served from the kernel
    └── routes.py      the routes
```

## Add a package

```sh
uv run xtr-recipes recipes:add xtr-cache
```

It installs the package and applies its recipe — the bundle, its configuration file, its
environment variables — and prints any step left to do by hand. `xtr.lock` records what was
applied; commit it.

## Check

```sh
uv run pytest
uv run ruff check && uv run ruff format --check
uv run basedpyright && uv run ty check
uv run xtr-recipes recipes:sync --check
```
